{
  "version": 1,
  "mode": "play",
  "comment": "The calculator's faceplate mirrors the HARDWARE: every button is bound to its circuit part (a widget press IS the board button's press, through board.setControl), and the display is bound to the circuit's SSD1306 — the widget shows the device's actual GDDRAM pixels, not a text copy. Loading the example applies this layout; nothing here needs the program's variables.",
